  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing movement data management for humanitarian response in the Democratic Republic of the Congo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) continues to face multiple conflicts that have created one of the world&#x2019;s most complex and persistent crisis leading to significant humanitarian needs. In the eastern provinces, armed conflicts and insecurity prevail in several areas across Ituri, North Kivu, and South Kivu.To address the extensive crisis impacting the Democratic Republic of the Congo and the substantial shifts in the context, IOM&apos;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) is enhancing access to comprehensive data on displaced and returned populations, needs, and vulnerabilities for improved response efforts. This will allow the humanitarian community and local actors to undertake well-informed coordination, response planning, and assistance to displaced populations.</narrative>
  </description>
